{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"039f1b4d0cebe27bde749160","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260813042012.17631-1-phucduc.bui%40gmail.com/","channels":["linux-arm-msm"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260813042012.17631-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260813042012.17631-1-phucduc.bui%40gmail.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260813042012.17631-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 1/2] net: xilinx: axienet: Propagate errors from optional IRQ lookup","messages":{"20260814170001.GQ265046@horms.kernel.org":{"id":"20260814170001.GQ265046@horms.kernel.org","messageId":"20260814170001.GQ265046@horms.kernel.org","references":["20260813042012.17631-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260813042012.17631-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"],"author":{"name":"Simon Horman","address":"horms@kernel.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"","address":"phucduc.bui@gmail.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"Radhey Shyam Pandey","address":"radhey.shyam.pandey@amd.com"},{"name":"Andrew Lunn","address":"andrew+netdev@lunn.ch"},{"name":"Eric Dumazet","address":"edumazet@google.com"},{"name":"Jakub Kicinski","address":"kuba@kernel.org"},{"name":"Paolo Abeni","address":"pabeni@redhat.com"},{"name":"Michal Simek","address":"michal.simek@amd.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"netdev@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T17:00:01.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T17:00:01.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 1/2] net: xilinx: axienet: Propagate errors from optional IRQ lookup","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Thu, Aug 13, 2026 at 11:20:11AM +0700, phucduc.bui@gmail.com wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"From: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"platform_get_irq_optional() returns a positive IRQ number on success or"},{"depth":1,"text":"a negative error code on failure. For an optional IRQ, -ENXIO indicates"},{"depth":1,"text":"that no optional IRQ is available, while other errors should be propagated."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Propagate all error codes returned by platform_get_irq_optional() other"},{"depth":1,"text":"than -ENXIO."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Another call to platform_get_irq_optional() in the same function already"},{"depth":1,"text":"handles the return value this way. Apply the same error handling to this"},{"depth":1,"text":"call site for consistency."}],"lineCount":12,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"It would be useful to explain how this problem was discovered,\nand what testing the patch has seen. Please add an Assisted-by\ntag if appropriate."},{"kind":"code","text":"Link: https://docs.kernel.org/process/coding-assistants.html"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c | 4 ++++"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index fcf517069d16..d23e9796725d 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -2957,12 +2957,16 @@ static int axienet_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\tlp->tx_irq = irq_of_parse_and_map(np, 0);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\tof_node_put(np);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\tlp->eth_irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 0);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tif (lp->eth_irq < 0 && lp->eth_irq != -ENXIO)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\treturn lp->eth_irq;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t} else {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t/* Check for these resources directly on the Ethernet node. */"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\tlp->dma_regs = devm_platform_get_and_ioremap_resource(pdev, 1, NULL);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\tlp->rx_irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 1);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\tlp->tx_irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\tlp->eth_irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 2);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tif (lp->eth_irq < 0 && lp->eth_irq != -ENXIO)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\treturn lp->eth_irq;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t}"}],"lineCount":25,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The same check seems to have been added to both arms of the if/else\ncondition. So it seems to me that it could be moved out of that condition."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I would suggest placing it below the existing rx_irq/tx_irq condition\nwhich appears a few lines below this hunk so that those and\ndma_regs errors are still propagated."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":" \t\tif (IS_ERR(lp->dma_regs)) {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\tdev_err(&pdev->dev, \"could not map DMA regs\\n\");"},{"depth":1,"text":"-- "},{"depth":1,"text":"2.43.0"},{"depth":1,"text":""}],"lineCount":5,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260813042012.17631-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com"},"CAABR9nFxfzf8QP-wq5iaJRTL+HG+a+tNqqX2daj-=Cwp46hPJQ@mail.gmail.com":{"id":"CAABR9nFxfzf8QP-wq5iaJRTL+HG+a+tNqqX2daj-=Cwp46hPJQ@mail.gmail.com","messageId":"CAABR9nFxfzf8QP-wq5iaJRTL+HG+a+tNqqX2daj-=Cwp46hPJQ@mail.gmail.com","references":["20260813042012.17631-1-phucduc.bui@gmail.com","20260814170001.GQ265046@horms.kernel.org"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Bui Duc Phuc","address":"phucduc.bui@gmail.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Simon Horman","address":"horms@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Radhey Shyam Pandey","address":"radhey.shyam.pandey@amd.com"},{"name":"Andrew Lunn","address":"andrew+netdev@lunn.ch"},{"name":"Eric Dumazet","address":"edumazet@google.com"},{"name":"Jakub Kicinski","address":"kuba@kernel.org"},{"name":"Paolo Abeni","address":"pabeni@redhat.com"},{"name":"Michal Simek","address":"michal.simek@amd.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"netdev@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-15T03:13:59.000Z","iso":"2026-08-15T03:13:59.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 1/2] net: xilinx: axienet: Propagate errors from optional IRQ lookup","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi Simon,"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thank you for you review"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"It would be useful to explain how this problem was discovered,"},{"depth":1,"text":"and what testing the patch has seen. Please add an Assisted-by"},{"depth":1,"text":"tag if appropriate."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Link: https://docs.kernel.org/process/coding-assistants.html"},{"depth":1,"text":""}],"lineCount":7,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Greg Kroah-Hartman previously asked about how this issue was discovered\nand how the patch was tested, and I provided the details here:"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"https://lore.kernel.org/all/CAABR9nEfPqXAt8wDo597qDS3b3KMaHeF6-swAFg9RLanapDnBQ@mail.gmail.com/"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Regarding AI assistance, I addressed the same question from another\nmaintainer here:"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"https://lore.kernel.org/all/CAABR9nFgiNv6cnYa3+ZY3KnjbKpcF-JHpZY8TVcR7H40vOoR=Q@mail.gmail.com/"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The answers are the same in both cases, so I hope it is okay to refer\nto those replies\nrather than repeating the same information here."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"The same check seems to have been added to both arms of the if/else"},{"depth":1,"text":"condition. So it seems to me that it could be moved out of that condition."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I would suggest placing it below the existing rx_irq/tx_irq condition"},{"depth":1,"text":"which appears a few lines below this hunk so that those and"},{"depth":1,"text":"dma_regs errors are still propagated."},{"depth":1,"text":""}],"lineCount":8,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Previously, I understood that errors should be returned as early as possible.\nHowever, with the current implementation, I agree that your approach\nmakes more sense.\nI’ll send v3 soon."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Best regards,\nPhuc"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260814170001.GQ265046@horms.kernel.org","parentId":"20260814170001.GQ265046@horms.kernel.org"}},"rootIds":["20260814170001.GQ265046@horms.kernel.org"],"childrenByParent":{"20260814170001.GQ265046@horms.kernel.org":["CAABR9nFxfzf8QP-wq5iaJRTL+HG+a+tNqqX2daj-=Cwp46hPJQ@mail.gmail.com"]},"chronologicalIds":["20260814170001.GQ265046@horms.kernel.org","CAABR9nFxfzf8QP-wq5iaJRTL+HG+a+tNqqX2daj-=Cwp46hPJQ@mail.gmail.com"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}